// A borrowed function reference handed in as a parameter is not stored into a place reached through a
// call's result: nothing says the place does not live as long as the program, so it is held to the global
// lifetime, and the parameter's is the caller's.
//
// Verdict: refuse, ErrorInvType (1013) at the store.
// Basis: the invariant (doc/design/references-and-regions.md, "Lifetimes: one invariant"): whatever holds a
// borrow must not outlive its referent, and a place with no variable at its root is the global one. Lane 710:
// the scope was never written for such a root (an uninitialised read), so Windows accepted and Linux refused
// the same source; this case runs on both systems and must give the same verdict.

mod lifetime_band_store_callresult_fn_param_refused;

struct Globals { n: i32; hook: &fn(); }

fn glob() *Globals { null as *Globals }

pub fn setHook(f: &fn()) {
  (*glob()).hook = f;   //~ ErrorInvType
}

fn main() i32 { 0 }
